[{"figure_index": 1, "page_no": 40, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific figure labeled **a–d** describing a multimodal, multispecies biological foundation model workflow for brain single-cell/spatial data.\n\n**Panel a:** Circular multilayer summary plot of dataset composition. Rings encode categories including **Modality**, **Species**, **Age group**, **Region**, and **Disease**. Visible labels include:\n- Modalities: epigenomics, transcriptomics, spatial, transcriptomics\n- Species: mouse, marmoset, macaque, human\n- Age groups: prenatal, juvenile, adult, aged\n- Brain regions: entorhinal cortex, frontal cortex, insular cortex, occipital cortex, parietal cortex, retrosplenial cortex, subcortex, superior temporal cortex, temporal cortex, and other abbreviated regions\n- Disease categories: brain tumors, cognitive dysfunction, epilepsy, immune disorders, neurodegeneration, normal, others, psychiatric\n\n**Panel b:** Word-cloud summaries for metadata fields. Six labeled word clouds show prominent terms for:\n- Question type\n- Class\n- Subclass\n- Region\n- Age group\n- Disease  \nVisible frequent terms include **GABA**, **GL**, **oligo**, **Astro**, **Vip**, **Pvalb**, **cerebral cortex**, **frontal**, **temporal**, **aged**, **Normal**, **disease**, and **Alzheimer**.\n\n**Panel c:** Main model architecture and task interface. Biological inputs are shown as **cell and feature input** from **multi-omics** and **multi-species** sources, represented by molecular/omics icons and species silhouettes including mouse, monkey/primate, and human. The pipeline proceeds through:\n- Tokenization\n- Gene Encoder\n- Projector\n- Graph Convolutional Networks, labeled as **2 layers**\n- Learnable query\n- Cross attention\n- Large language model\n- Text input and text output interface\n\nThe right side shows six example question-answer task panels:\n1. **Cell type annotation:** asks what cell type corresponds to a gene expression pattern; answer says astrocyte.\n2. **Cell origin prediction:** predicts conserved or species-specific cell origin; answer indicates a primate-specific cell type.\n3. **Aging clock:** predicts age from feature abundance; answer gives biological age as 90 years old.\n4. **Disease status inference:** asks whether the cell is involved in Alzheimer’s disease pathogenesis; answer says the cell belongs to an AD-related subpopulation.\n5. **Gene mask prediction:** masked genes are predicted in expression order; visible answer lists **Gad1, Gad2, Atf4, Neurod1, Syt**.\n6. **Spatial mask prediction:** predicts top genes for neighboring spatial spots; visible answer lists **Gad1, Gad2, Atf4, Neurod1, Syt**.\n\n**Panel d:** Training strategy with two stages:\n- **Stage 1:** Cell & feature input passes through a frozen gene encoder, a trainable projector, text input, and a frozen LLM.\n- **Stage 2:** Cell & feature input passes through a trainable gene encoder, trainable projector, text input, and an LLM with LoRA.\n\nOverall, the figure presents dataset metadata distributions, task/category vocabulary, a biological feature-to-language model architecture, example biomedical question-answer tasks, and a two-stage training scheme for integrating gene/cell features with a large language model."]}, {"figure_index": 2, "page_no": 41, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure about single-cell/spatial omics cell-type prediction with a model named **scMOBA**.\n\nVisible content:\n- **Panel a:** Schematic model/interface workflow. A chat-style user asks about uploaded mouse **snATAC-seq** cells and **Stereo-seq** macaque cells. The system answers predicted biological identities such as **glutamatergic neurons**, **L6 IT Car3 subclass**, and **Lamp5 subclass**. Diagram shows scMOBA mapping cells into labeled cell types A/B/C and producing cell-type predictions.\n- **Panel b:** Horizontal bar chart reporting overall metrics: **Accuracy 0.9909**, **Precision macro 0.9379**, **Recall macro 0.8699**, **F1 macro 0.8715**.\n- **Panel c:** UMAP comparison of **Original** vs **Predicted** cell-type labels. Legend includes neuronal and non-neuronal classes such as **L2/3 IT, L5 IT, L6 IT, L6 IT Car3, L6b, L5/6 NP, L5 ET, L6 CT, VLMC, Micro/PVM, SST, VIP, PVALB, SNCG, LAMP5, Astro, Oligo, OPC, Endo**.\n- **Panel d:** Confusion matrix with **Predicted Labels** versus **Reference Labels**, showing strong diagonal agreement across the same cell-type categories.\n- **Panel e:** Alluvial/stacked flow plots comparing **Original** and **Predicted** labels for datasets **Mouse_Renbing2023_ATAC** and **Human_Pan2024_RNA**. Cell-type groups include **Astro, Bergmann glia, Choroid Plexus, Ependymal, GABA, GLU, Micro/PVM, Oligo, OPC, Vascular**.\n- **Panel f:** Dataset-level metric table with green bubble values for **Human_Agarwa2020_RNA**, **Human_Pan2024_RNA**, **Mouse_Renbing2023_ATAC**, and **Mouse_Wang2023_spatial**, reporting accuracy, macro precision, macro recall, and macro F1.\n- **Panel g:** Spatial tissue maps with predicted cortical layer/cell-type labels, including **L2/3 IT, L4 IT, L5 IT, L5/6 NP, L5 ET, L6 CT, L6 IT, L6b**, with accuracy values shown as **0.97** and **0.90**.\n- **Panel h:** Line plots comparing methods across species or datasets labeled **Human, Marmoset, Mouse**, with metrics **Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1**. Methods include **scMOBA**, **Geneformer**, and **scGPT**.\n- **Panel i:** Grouped bar chart comparing methods **scMOBA, scGPT, Geneformer, Seurat, Cell BLAST, scmap, SciBet** on **Accuracy, Precision macro, Recall macro, F1 score**.\n- **Panel j:** UMAP-style embedding with central clusters and zoomed dashed regions comparing **Original, scMOBA, Geneformer, scGPT** for cell subsets labeled **PVALB_2** and **L2/3 IT_3**.\n\nBiological source objects shown: single-cell nuclei/cells from mouse, human, marmoset, and macaque datasets; cortical neuronal subclasses; glial and vascular cell types; spatial transcriptomics spots/cells.\n\nMain finding visually conveyed: **scMOBA performs cell-type prediction across sequencing modalities and species, with high agreement to reference labels and stronger or comparable performance versus Geneformer, scGPT, and classical annotation methods.**"]}, {"figure_index": 3, "page_no": 42, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure about single-cell / spatial omics integration using **scMOBA**.\n\nPanels visible:\n\n- **a**: Schematic workflow. Labeled data are passed through **scMOBA** for integration. Unlabeled data are annotated by scMOBA, producing pseudolabeled data, then integrated again. Inputs and outputs are shown as dashed circular clusters containing different marker shapes/colors.\n- **b**: UMAP embeddings comparing methods: **scMOBA (label)**, **scMOBA (pseudolabel)**, **Geneformer**, and **scGPT**. Top row appears colored by dataset/modality, bottom row by cell type. Axes labeled **UMAP_1** and **UMAP_2**. Legend includes datasets **snRNA_1** and **snRNA_2**, and many cell types including L2/3 IT, L5 IT, L5/6 NP, L6 CT, VIP, OPC, Oligo, Astro, Micro/PVM, Endo, and others.\n- **c**: Quantitative benchmark table with bubble/circle scores for **Bio conservation**, **Batch correction**, and **Total**. Methods include **scMOBA (label)**, **scMOBA (pseudolabel)**, **Geneformer**, **scGPT**, **RPCA**, **CCA**, **FastMNN**, **scVI**, and **Harmony**. Metrics include **NMI**, **ARI**, **ASW cell-type**, **GC**, and **ASW batch**. scMOBA label has the highest visible total score, **0.94**.\n- **d**: Cross-species UMAP-style embeddings. Left panels compare **scMOBA (label)** and **scMOBA (pseudolabel)** with total scores **0.89** and **0.82**. Right panels show species-separated views labeled **Human**, **Marmoset**, **Macaque**, and **Chimpanzee**, colored by cell type. Cell-type legend includes IT subtypes, L6 CT, VIP, LAMP5, PVALB, SST, Astro, Endo, VLMC, Immune, Oligo, OPC, Micro, SMC, RB, and others.\n- **e**: Spatial/snRNA integration UMAP comparisons for **scMOBA (label)**, **scMOBA (pseudolabel)**, **RPCA**, **fastMNN**, **scVI**, and **Harmony**. Top row appears colored by modality, bottom row by cell type. Legend lists cell types **GABA**, **GLU**, **Astro**, **OPC**, **Oligo**, **Vascular** and modalities **spatial** and **snRNA**.\n- **f**: Benchmark table for panel e-like task. Metrics include bio conservation and batch correction. scMOBA label total score is **0.88**; scMOBA pseudolabel total is **0.84**.\n- **g**: Another benchmark table with the same method set and metric categories. scMOBA label and pseudolabel both show total score **0.51**, with other methods lower or comparable depending on metric.\n\nBiological source objects shown: single-cell or spatial transcriptomic embeddings of brain/cortical cell populations, including neuronal subtypes, glia, vascular/endothelial, immune, and species-level datasets from human, marmoset, macaque, and chimpanzee.\n\nMain visible finding: **scMOBA**, especially the label-supervised version, generally shows stronger integration and biological conservation scores than Geneformer, scGPT, and several classical integration methods across the displayed benchmarks."]}, {"figure_index": 4, "page_no": 43, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure labeled **a-k** about **scMOBA** for single-cell/cell-type annotation across species and brain cell types.\n\nPanel details:\n- **a**: Workflow schematic. Input data from animal/cell icons enters a model labeled **scMOBA** for **zero-shot prediction**. A second workflow shows **fine-tuning** using **reference data**, then **transfer weights** to annotate **query data**, producing **cell type annotation**. Biological source objects are illustrated as animal silhouettes and colored cell/tissue-like icons.\n- **b**: Four-petal metric diagram for **Chimpanzee**, showing **F1 0.9761**, **Accuracy 0.9884**, **Recall 0.9920**, and **Precision 0.9649**.\n- **c**: Confusion-matrix heatmap comparing **original labels** and **predicted labels** for broad brain cell types: Astro, GABA, GLU, Micro/PVM, Oligo, OPC, Vascular.\n- **d**: Bar chart for **Chimpanzee** metrics: Accuracy **0.8695**, Precision **0.6856**, Recall **0.7387**, F1 score **0.6779**.\n- **e**: Larger confusion-matrix heatmap for finer cell labels including Astro, Oligo, OPC, Endo, VLMC, Micro/PVM, L2/3 IT, L4 IT, L5 IT, L5 ET, L5/6 NP, L6 IT, L6b, L6 CT, LAMP5, LAMP5 LHX6, PVALB, SST, VIP, PAX6, SNCG.\n- **f**: Sankey/alluvial plots for **Lizard** and **Turtle**, comparing **Original** to **Predicted** cell-type assignments. Legend includes Neural progenitor cell, Astro, Ependymoglial, GABA, GLU, Micro/PVM, Oligo, OPC, Vascular.\n- **g**: Violin/ridge-like expression plots for marker genes **GFAP** and **SLC1A2**, comparing **Lizard** and **Turtle** across cell types.\n- **h**: Gene ontology/enrichment-style horizontal bar chart with terms such as **Glial cell differentiation**, **Cerebral cortex development**, **Astrocyte differentiation**, **Regulation of nervous system development**, and **Pallium development**, plotted by **-logP**.\n- **i**: Four bar charts comparing **Marmoset**, **Macaque**, and **Chimpanzee** for Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1, with scores around 0.94-0.97.\n- **j**: Line chart comparing annotation methods across primates. Methods listed: **Cell BLAST**, **Geneformer**, **scMOBA**, **scGPT**, **SciBet**, **scmap**. Y-axis is Accuracy.\n- **k**: Two clustered heatmaps with dendrograms and animal icons. Left appears human-to-primate comparison; right appears mouse-to-primate comparison. Heatmaps show group probabilities for **Group2**, **Group4**, and **Group3**, with columns labeled by developmental/stage-like sample names."]}, {"figure_index": 5, "page_no": 44, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure labeled **a-j** about single-cell/molecular age prediction from gene expression, with biological cell-type analyses and spatial age maps.\n\nVisible content:\n- **Panel a:** Schematic of a model interface named **scMOBA**. Input examples show natural-language questions and answers about age prediction from gene expression profiles, including a human query and a mouse query. The diagram connects gene-expression/cell representations to an **Age Prediction** output with stages labeled **Infant, Child, Adolescent, Adult, Elderly** and mouse age icons.\n- **Panel b:** Scatter plots of **predicted age vs actual/microarray age** for cell types: **Astrocyte, Endothelial, Excitatory neuron, Inhibitory neuron, Microglia, Oligodendrocyte, OPC**. Pearson correlations are shown, mostly near **1.000**, with Microglia lower at **0.995**. Points are colored by functional/pathway categories listed in the legend, including blood vessel diameter maintenance, cytokine signaling in immune system, interferon alpha/beta signaling, MAPK family signaling cascades, and vascular process in circulatory system.\n- **Panel c:** Confusion-matrix-like heatmap comparing **Predicted** vs **Original** age classes: **Adult, Elderly, Infant**. Strong diagonal values are visible, including **0.98 Adult**, **0.95 Elderly**, and **0.96 Infant**.\n- **Panel d:** Radial/petal plot showing cell-type prediction scores or correlations for **Oligodendrocyte, Astrocyte, Endothelial, Excitatory neuron, Inhibitory neuron, Microglia, OPC**, with values such as **0.947**, **0.868**, **0.804**, **0.802**, **0.870**.\n- **Panel e:** Gene/network visualization for **Endothelial** cells. Labeled genes include **FN1, PDGFRB, CLDN5, TEK, CALM1, ACTB, SPTBN1, IFITM3, SLC2A1, SLC1A3, ABCG2, HSP90AA1, B2M, VIM**, and others. Nodes are connected by gray edges.\n- **Panel f:** Multiple scatter plots of **Median Pred Value** vs **Answer Value** for cell types including **Astrocyte, Endothelial, Ependymal, Microglia, NSC, Neuroblast, Neuron-Excitatory, Neuron-Inhibitory, Neuron-MSN, OPC, Oligodendrocyte, Pericyte, VLMC, VSMC**. Each has a red regression line and shaded **95% CI** with Pearson r values.\n- **Panel g:** Density plots comparing predicted age distributions for **Old** vs **Young** groups across cell types: **Astrocyte, Endothelial, Ependymal, Microglia, Neuron, Oligodendrocyte, OPC, Pericyte, VSMC**.\n- **Panel h:** Spatial/tissue section maps with a color bar labeled **Age (months)** ranging approximately **0 to 35**, and examples labeled by **True age**: **3.8, 8.6, 19.8, 26.7** months. A **1 mm** scale bar is shown.\n- **Panel i:** Radial gene ontology enrichment visualization labeled **GO Enrichment Terms**, with clusters including **response to growth factor**, **positive regulation of cytokine production**, **neuroinflammation and glutamatergic signaling**, and **positive regulation of canonical NF-kappaB signal transduction**. Gene names radiate from colored enrichment nodes.\n- **Panel j:** Heatmaps comparing differences across cell types and brain regions under **Yamanaka factors** and **Exercise**. Rows include the same neural/glial/vascular cell types, and columns/regions include **CC/ACO, CTX, STR, VEN**. Color scales show positive and negative differences.\n\nOverall finding represented visually: the figure presents a multimodal/single-cell age-prediction framework that predicts biological age across human/mouse expression profiles and cell types, evaluates accuracy with correlations and class prediction matrices, identifies cell-type-specific gene networks and GO terms, maps predicted age spatially in tissue sections, and compares interventions such as Yamanaka factors and exercise."]}, {"figure_index": 6, "page_no": 47, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel biomedical/AI figure labeled **a-d**.\n\n**Panel a:** Stacked bar charts summarizing cell counts in millions. Left chart groups by modality: **RNA**, **ATAC**, and **Spatial**, with stacked species categories **Human**, **Mouse**, **Macaque**, **Marmoset**. Right chart groups by species: **Human**, **Mouse**, **Macaque**, **Marmoset**, with stacked omics categories **RNA**, **ATAC**, **Spatial**. Total shown as **129.6M** cells.\n\n**Panel b:** Pie charts describing dataset composition. Categories include **Disease**, **Region**, and **Development stage**. Disease includes **Normal**, **Neurodegeneration**, **Brain Tumors**, **Epilepsy**, **Immune disorders**, **Cognitive impairment**, **Psychiatric**, and **Other**. Region includes **Subcortex**, **Frontal Cortex**, **Temporal Cortex**, **Precentral Cortex**, **Occipital Cortex**, **Insular Cortex**, **Entorhinal Cortex**, **Retrosplenial Cortex**, and **Other cortex**, with an inset breakdown for subcortical regions. Development stage includes **Infancy**, **Adolescence**, **Adult**, **Elderly**, and fetal trimester stages.\n\n**Panel c:** Three Sankey/alluvial-style mappings comparing **Original** cell-type annotations to **Consensus** labels for brain cell classes. Subpanels are labeled **GABA DA**, **GLU**, and **NN**. Visible biological labels include neuronal and non-neuronal types such as **MSN**, **BG GABA**, **Chandelier**, **Pvalb**, **Sst**, **Vip**, **L5/6 NP**, **L6 CT**, **CB GLU**, **HP-SUB GLU**, **OPC**, **SMC**, **Astro**, **Bergmann glia**, **Micro/PVM**, and **Oligo**. Dataset label visible under the GLU mapping: **Human_Renbin2023_ATAC**.\n\n**Panel d:** Workflow/model architecture diagram. Input is a cell-by-feature matrix with modalities labeled **Spatial Transcriptomics**, **Epigenomics**, and **Transcriptomics**. The workflow includes **Tokenization**, a **Gene Encoder**, a **GCN Module** using **Spectral Graph Conv**, a **Learnable Query** block with **Cross Attention**, optional **Text Input** embedding, **Concat**, and an interface to a **Large language model (Llama-3.2-1B)**. Example prompt asks what cell type corresponds to a gene expression pattern, with example output stating the cell type is **astrocyte**."]}, {"figure_index": 7, "page_no": 48, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel biological machine learning figure with panels labeled **a-f**.\n\nPanel **a** shows two UMAP embeddings labeled **Original** and **Predicted**, comparing cell-type distributions. Axes are **UMAP_1** and **UMAP_2**. Cell types in the legend include **Astro**, **GABA**, **GLU**, **Micro/PVM**, **Oligo**, **OPC**, and **Vascular**. Labels are placed near clusters such as GLU, OPC, Astro, Oligo, Vascular, GABA, and Micro/PVM.\n\nPanel **b** is a red heatmap with a 0.0-1.0 color scale, showing marker-like gene expression or scores across cell classes. Column labels include neuronal and glial categories such as **L2/3 IT**, **L5 ET**, **L5/6 NP**, **L6 IT**, **L6b**, **PVALB**, **SST**, **VIP**, **SNCG**, **Astro**, **Oligo**, **OPC**, and **Micro**. Row gene labels visible include **CADM2**, **DPP10**, **NRG1**, **HS3ST4**, **SOX5**, **TLE4**, **SYT2**, **SST**, **GAD1**, **CXCL14**, **GFAP**, **SLC1A2**, **S100B**, **PLP1**, **PTN**, **CX3CR1**, **P2RY12**, and **CSF1R**.\n\nPanel **c** contains two enrichment scatterplots titled **L2/3 IT** and **ASC**. The x-axis is **Enrichment Score**, and point color encodes **-log10(P-value)**. Enrichment terms shown include axonogenesis, neuron projection morphogenesis, regulation of synapse organization, regulation of membrane potential, modulation of chemical synaptic transmission, regulation of gliogenesis, glial cell differentiation, cell-cell adhesion, and regulation of neurogenesis.\n\nPanel **d** shows UMAP embeddings for **marmoset** and **mouse**, each comparing **Original** and **Predicted** cell-type annotations. The legend includes many cortical cell classes: **Astro**, **Endo**, **L2/3 IT**, **L5 ET**, **L5 IT**, **L5/6 NP**, **L6 CT**, **L6 IT**, **L6 IT Car3**, **L6b**, **LAMP5**, **Micro/PVM**, **OPC**, **Oligo**, **PVALB**, **SNCG**, **SST**, **SST CHODL**, **VLMC**, **VIP**, **Peri**, **MEIS2**, and **SMC**.\n\nPanel **e** shows four line plots: **Accuracy**, **Precision**, **Recall**, and **F1**, plotted against **Training Ratio (%)**. Methods compared are **scMOBA**, **GeneFormer**, and **scGPT**. Species are indicated by marker shapes for **Human**, **Marmoset**, and **Mouse**.\n\nPanel **f** shows a grid of UMAP-style feature or class localization plots comparing rows **Original**, **scMOBA**, **Geneformer**, and **scGPT**. Columns include cell classes **L2/3 IT_13**, **L5 IT_5**, **L5 IT_6**, **L6 CT_1**, **L6 IT Car3_2**, **L6b_2**, **LAMP5_5**, **PVALB_10**, and **SST_9**. Blue points mark selected class locations over gray background cells.\n\nOverall, the figure appears to evaluate predicted versus original single-cell or single-nucleus transcriptomic cell-type annotations across human, marmoset, and mouse brain/cortical datasets, comparing models including **scMOBA**, **GeneFormer**, and **scGPT** using UMAP visualizations, marker heatmaps, enrichment analysis, and classification metrics."]}, {"figure_index": 8, "page_no": 49, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel scientific figure showing UMAP embeddings for single-cell/spatial omics integration and model comparisons.\n\nPanel details:\n- **a**: Five columns labeled **Harmony**, **RPCA**, **CCA**, **FastMNN**, and **scVI**. Each method shows paired UMAP plots: top colored by dataset/modality and bottom colored by cell type. Legend includes datasets **snRNA_1** and **snRNA_2**, and many cortical/neural cell types such as **L2/3 IT**, **L5 IT**, **L6 IT**, **PVALB**, **SNCG**, **Astro**, **VLMC**, **L5 ET**, **L5/6 NP**, **L6 CT**, **VIP**, **LAMP5**, **Oligo**, **Micro/PVM**, **L6 IT Car3**, **L6b**, **SST**, **OPC**, **SST CHODL**, and **Endo**.\n- **b**: UMAP comparison of **Unintegrated** versus **Integrated** data. Top row appears colored by modality/dataset; bottom row colored by cell type. Cell type legend includes **GABA**, **GLU**, **Astro**, **OPC**, **Oligo**, and **Vascular**. Modality legend includes **spatial** and **snRNA**.\n- **c**: Side-by-side comparison of **Geneformer** and **scGPT** embeddings, with “Total 0.39” and “Total 0.78” shown above them. Rows are labeled by species/source: **Human**, **Marmoset**, **Macaque**, and **Chimpanzee**. Points are colored by cell type, with a large legend including excitatory neuron subclasses, interneuron subclasses, glia, vascular, immune, and other cell classes.\n- **d**: UMAP comparison of **Geneformer** and **scGPT** for multimodal data. Top row colored by modality, bottom row colored by cell type. Modalities include **snRNA** and **snATAC**; cell types include **GABA**, **GLU**, **Astro**, **OPC**, **Oligo**, and **Vascular**.\n- **e**: Wide comparison across methods: **scMOBA (label)**, **scMOBA (pseudolabel)**, **scGPT**, **Geneformer**, **Harmony**, **RPCA**, **CCA**, **FastMNN**, and **scVI**. Each method has two UMAPs: top colored by cell type and bottom colored by modality. Modalities include **snRNA** and **spatial**.\n\nBiological/source objects:\n- Single-cell or spatial transcriptomic/omics observations from brain/cortical tissue.\n- Cell categories include excitatory and inhibitory neurons, astrocytes, oligodendrocytes, OPCs, vascular cells, microglia/immune cells, and endothelial/perivascular classes.\n- Cross-species comparison includes human, marmoset, macaque, and chimpanzee.\n\nTransformations/model interfaces:\n- Dimensionality reduction visualized as **UMAP_1** and **UMAP_2**.\n- Integration/batch-correction or representation methods compared: **Harmony**, **RPCA**, **CCA**, **FastMNN**, **scVI**, **Geneformer**, **scGPT**, and **scMOBA**.\n- Modalities compared include **snRNA**, **spatial**, and **snATAC**.\n\nVisible findings:\n- The figure visually compares how well different methods mix datasets/modalities while preserving cell-type structure.\n- **scGPT** appears to produce more separated cell-type clusters than **Geneformer** in panels c and d.\n- Integration methods vary in modality mixing and cluster separation across panels a, b, and e."]}, {"figure_index": 9, "page_no": 50, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel biological/computational figure about cell-type label prediction/classification across species or datasets.\n\nVisible content:\n- Panel **a**: Venn-style metric summary for **Rhesus macaque**, showing **Accuracy 0.9959**, **Precision 0.9962**, **Recall 0.9928**, and **F1 0.9944**.\n- Panel **b**: Confusion matrix titled **Original labels**, comparing predicted and original broad cell labels: **Astro, GABA, GLU, Micro/PVM, Oligo, OPC, Vascular**. Most values lie on the diagonal, indicating high classification agreement.\n- Panel **c**: Bar chart for **Rhesus macaque** with scores: **Accuracy 0.8342**, **Precision 0.7145**, **Recall 0.6949**, **F1 Score 0.6535**.\n- Panel **d**: Larger confusion matrix titled **Original labels**, comparing fine-grained neural/cell labels including **Astro, Oligo, OPC, Endo, VLMC, Micro/PVM, L2/3 IT, L4 IT, L5 IT, L5 ET, L5/6 NP, L6 IT, L6b, L6 CT, LAMP5, LAMP5 LHX6, PVALB, SST, VIP, PAX6, SNCG**. Predicted labels are on the y-axis; original labels on the x-axis. Strong diagonal structure is visible with some off-diagonal confusion.\n- Panel **e**: UMAP scatter plots comparing **Original** and **Predicted** annotations for **Lizard** and **Turtle**. Legend includes **Neural progenitor cell, Astro, Ependymoglial, GABA, GLU, Micro/PVM, Oligo, OPC, Vascular**.\n- Panel **f**: Violin plots of **GAD2** expression across cell types, with strongest signal in **GABA** cells for both displayed rows.\n- Panel **g**: Enrichment-style horizontal bar plot with **−logP** scale. Terms shown include **Nervous system development**, **Axon guidance**, **Organelle localization**, and **Regulation of neuronal synaptic plasticity**.\n- Panel **h**: Heatmaps showing probabilities for groups **GroupA, GroupB, GroupC**, with silhouettes/icons suggesting comparisons involving human and non-human primate contexts. Labels include cortical/neural subtype-like entries such as **L5/6**, **L4**, and many numbered **CTX** labels.\n\nBiological source objects visible:\n- Neural and glial cell classes, including excitatory/inhibitory neurons and non-neuronal brain cell types.\n- Species explicitly shown: **Rhesus macaque**, **Lizard**, **Turtle**.\n- Marker gene shown: **GAD2**.\n\nTransformations/model-interface evidence:\n- Original labels are compared to predicted labels through confusion matrices.\n- UMAP embeddings visualize original versus predicted cell-type annotations.\n- Probability heatmaps indicate model/group assignment outputs.\n- Performance metrics summarize classification quality.\n\nMain visible finding:\n- The model appears to accurately recover broad and fine cell-type labels, with high diagonal agreement in confusion matrices, strong GAD2 association with GABA cells, and predicted labels broadly matching original UMAP structure across lizard and turtle datasets."]}, {"figure_index": 10, "page_no": 51, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nMulti-panel biological network and heatmap figure labeled **a-g**.\n\nPanel **a**: Clustered heatmap with row dendrogram on the left and a color scale from **0.0 to 1.0** on the right. Columns are grouped by age-stage labels across the top: **20-year-old stage**, **25-year-old stage**, **68-year-old stage**, and **70-year-old stage**. The heatmap shows age-associated block patterns, with younger stages differing from older stages in intensity structure.\n\nPanels **b-g**: Cell-type-specific gene/protein interaction or pathway networks, each with labeled nodes, grey connecting edges, and colored nodes mapped to functional/pathway annotations in legends.\n\nPanel **b**: **Excitatory neuron** network. Visible genes include synaptic and neuronal markers such as **GRIN2A, GRIA2, GRIA4, CAMK2A, DLG2, SNAP25, CACNA1C, TRPC1, NDUFS1, NDUFA10**. Legend categories include **Glutamatergic synapse**, **Pathways of neurodegeneration - multiple diseases**, **Protein modification by small protein conjugation**, and **Unblocking of NMDA receptors, glutamate binding and activation**.\n\nPanel **c**: **Inhibitory neuron** network. Visible nodes include **GRIN2A, GRIA2, GRIA4, GRIK1, GABRA1, SNAP25, NRXN1, NLGN1, SYT1, KCNQ2, KCNQ3, KCNB2, CACNA1C**. Legend categories include **GABA synthesis, release, reuptake and degradation**, **Neurotransmitter secretion**, **Pathways of neurodegeneration - multiple diseases**, and **Potassium ion transport**.\n\nPanel **d**: **Microglia** network. Visible nodes include **SNAP25, ACTG1, TUBA1B, AKT3, CREBBP, CLU, CUL5, SPP1, ARIH1, FOXD1, EIF4G3, PSPC1**. Legend categories include **Activation of immune response**, **Cellular response to cytokine stimulus**, **Cytokine signaling in immune system**, and **TYROBP causal network in microglia**.\n\nPanel **e**: **Astrocyte** network. Visible nodes include **GAPDH, UBC, RPS27A, ACTB, GFAP, GRIA2, NCAM1, LRP1, APC, UQCRB, NDUFA4, CAMK2G**. Legend categories include **Alzheimer disease**, **Inflammatory mediator regulation of TRP channels**, **Neuron projection development**, **Parkinson disease**, and **Pathways of neurodegeneration - multiple diseases**.\n\nPanel **f**: **Oligodendrocyte** network. Visible nodes include **APP, HSP90AA1, TUBA1A, MAP1B, NTRK2, ERBB4, PTPRD, NLGN1, SNAP25, NRXN3, NF1**. Legend categories include **Cellular response to growth factor stimulus**, **Learning or memory**, **Neuron cell-cell adhesion**, and **Neuron migration**.\n\nPanel **g**: **OPC** network. Visible nodes include **NRXN1, NLGN1, DLG2, GRIA2, NCAM1, CNTNAP2, PTPRD, VCAN, NEGR1, SPARCL1, PCDH15**. Legend categories include **Cell-cell adhesion**, **Cell adhesion molecules**, and **Negative regulation of glial cell differentiation**.\n\nThe figure appears to summarize age-stage molecular patterns and cell-type-specific 